index ce090edce49bb9fce9846939f448a5d4ae0770e5..2e0d3d788dea855dadc3c2932616c81f6e86e2e0
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Backoffice dry-run validation is a side-effect-free `internal/controlplane/backoffice` service with optional read ports for existence/impact checks: malformed request shape returns typed API errors, while candidate configuration defects return a successful `yalla.output.v1` report with stable `warnings`, `blocking_errors`, and `simulated_organizations` arrays. Secret-looking credential values are rejected without echoing the submitted value.
 - Backoffice runtime configuration uses global `admin_config_sets` plus `admin_config_versions`, not tenant tables: create editable drafts, publish immutable effective-at versions, archive instead of deleting, and make runtime readers select only `status='published'` rows whose `effective_at` has passed. Bump the set `revision` on version mutations so future cache layers have a monotonic invalidation token.
 - Worker queue metrics follow the HTTP metrics collector shape: aggregate series by low-cardinality dimensions only (`event`, `job_type`, `status`, `status_class`), keep job/request/correlation/org/project/environment/service identifiers as latest-sample log-join hints, and emit worker events only after successful claim/outcome commits so metrics reflect durable queue state.
 - Billing-grade container metric stories follow the same four-piece tracked-metric vertical as Traefik/build metering: add a runtime `metering.MetricDefinition`, extend the closed `quota_resource` domain plus `store.QuotaResource`, quarantine samples before billing unless attribution resolves a full org/project/environment/service scope, and emit idempotent `usage_events` whose current-period aggregation is visible through the organization usage projection.

